  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Thirteen strikeouts and a single run doesn't build a losing streak. It confirms one.",
    "what_this_means": "The offense was erased before it had a chance to matter. Houser gave them everything a team could ask for in six innings, one earned run, and the bats answered with three hits and thirteen strikeouts. The kind of performance disparity that doesn't happen by accident. This is the Giants' season right now: pitching showing up, lineup leaving. They've scored one run in their last two games. They're 2-8 in their last ten. The margin for error vanished weeks ago, and games like this one. Where the pitcher did his job and nobody else showed up. Are the difference between a stumble and a collapse. The inconsistency that has haunted them all season isn't random anymore. It's the pattern.",
